ned in explanation b to  <b>Section</b> <b>126</b>  of the <b>Electricity</b> Act, 2003. Though", "docsize": 42006, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Allahabad High Court", "citation": "AIR 2012 ALLAHABAD 163"}, {"tid": 73490373, "catids": null, "doctype": 1017, "publishdate": "2022-08-10", "authorid": 792, "bench": [792], "title": "Ramjibhai Dayabhai Pansara vs Paschim Gujarat Vij Company Ltd on 10 August, 2022", "numcites": 11, "numcitedby": 1, "headline": "assessment by invoking power under  <b>Section</b> <b>126</b>(1)  of the Act, even in\n       cases where <b>electricity</b> is <b>unauthorisedly</b> <b>used</b> by way of theft. When ... under\n        <b>Section</b> <b>126</b>(1)  of the Act only. There is apparent distinction between\n        <b>Section</b> <b>126</b>  and  <b>Section</b> 135  of the Act.  <b>Section</b> <b>126</b>  forms part", "docsize": 21228, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Gujarat High Court", "author": "A S Supehia", "authorEncoded": "a-s-supehia"}, {"tid": 101650680, "catids": null, "doctype": 1013, "publishdate": "2016-07-14", "authorid": 1101, "bench": [1165, 1101], "title": "Jenin Mon V vs Kerala State <b>Electricity</b> Board Ltd on 14 July, 2016", "numcites": 9, "numcitedby": 2, "headline": "there was high instances of\n\n&#x27;<b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b>&#x27; of <b>electricity</b>, which came within the purview\n\nof  <b>Section</b> <b>126</b> ... that the primary object under  <b>Section</b> <b>126</b> \n\nis to ensure &#x27;stoppage of misuse/<b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b>&#x27; of <b>electricity</b>\n\nas well as &#x27;prevention", "docsize": 35926, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Kerala High Court", "author": "A Narendran", "authorEncoded": "a-narendran"}, {"tid": 188007563, "catids": null, "doctype": 1006, "publishdate": "2022-06-29", "authorid": null, "bench": null, "title": "Sk. Sahajahan Mondal vs The State Of West Bengal And Others on 29 June, 2022", "numcites": 7, "numcitedby": 2, "headline": "<b>Section</b> <b>126</b>(5)  specifically stipulates that if the\n\nassessing Officer reaches to the conclusion that\n\n<b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b> has taken place, the\n\nassessment shall ... during which such <b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b> has\n\ntaken place and if, however, the period during which\n\nsuch <b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b> has taken place", "docsize": 11797, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Calcutta High Court (Appellete Side)"}, {"tid": 931171, "catids": [7, 10, 4], "doctype": 1022, "publishdate": "2007-01-08", "authorid": 1552, "bench": [1552], "title": "Gopal Sao And Anr. vs State Of Bihar And Anr. on 8 January, 2007", "numcites": 10, "numcitedby": 2, "headline": "conclusion that <b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b> has taken place it shall be presumed that such <b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b> was continuing for a period ... been <b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b> then there would be presumption against offender that he has been making <b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> of the <b>electricity</b> continuing", "docsize": 11488, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Patna High Court", "author": "S P Singh", "authorEncoded": "s-p-singh"}, {"tid": 980761, "catids": null, "doctype": 1013, "publishdate": "2008-11-28", "authorid": 1686, "bench": [1686], "title": "M.S. Premkumar vs Kerala State <b>Electricity</b> Board on 28 November, 2008", "numcites": 7, "numcitedby": 1, "headline": "<b>electricity</b> charges.\n\nAssessment of <b>electricity</b> charges is the expression which is to be found in\n\n <b>Section</b> <b>126</b> .  <b>Section</b> <b>126</b>(1)  of the <b>Electricity</b> Act being ... such <b>use</b>.&quot;\n\n  No doubt the assessment of <b>electricity</b> charges in the case of <b>unauthorised</b>\n\n<b>use</b> as contemplated in  <b>Section</b> <b>126</b>", "docsize": 15956, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Kerala High Court", "author": "K Joseph", "a